== 3.19 Pan-Cohort Linearized Deconvolution Concordance with Single-Cell Milopy Abundance and Zero-Shot LOCO Transfer
A central methodological question of this study is whether cell-state responder associations inferred by bulk RNA-seq deconvolution ($hat(beta)_("deconv", k)$) in independent clinical trials agree directionally and quantitatively with continuous single-cell neighborhood differential abundance (`milopy` $overline("logFC")_k$) measured directly in patient biopsies. Crucially, after enforcing automated $log_2$-scale detection and exact linear TPM inversion ($2^X - 1 -> 10^6$ TPM), whole-tumor stromal background alignment for sorted leukocyte references, and cell-size $S_k$ correction (Section 2.14), cross-modality concordance between DerSimonian–Laird meta-analytic bulk effects (`Pan-iAtlas-Meta`, $N = 1,015$) and single-cell `milopy` $overline("logFC")_k$ was remarkably strong across all 13 references (@fig-iatlas-milo-concordance, @fig-iatlas-transfer-loco).

