Across all 13 single-cell references evaluated against `Pan-iAtlas-Meta` (@fig-iatlas-milo-concordance), Pearson linear correlation $r$ ranged from $+0.886$ (`CELLxGENE_6f9de485` TNBC @yan2026singlecell, Spearman $rho = +0.830$, $83.3%$ sign agreement) to $+0.987$ (`GSE233203` NSCLC @hong2025singlecell, $rho = +0.962$, $100.0%$ sign agreement across 34/34 states; all 13 references $p <= 5 times 10^(-4)$ by exact permutation test). Notable single-cohort and unified concordance benchmarks included:
- *Lung & Colorectal Tier 1A Atlases*: `GSE207422` @hu2023singlecell achieved $r = +0.980, rho = +0.983$ ($97.4%$ sign agreement, 37/38 states), `GSE243013` @liu2025multiomic achieved $r = +0.940, rho = +0.917$ ($90.9%$, 30/33), and `CELLxGENE_05a8c945` @marteau2026singlecell achieved $100.0%$ directional sign concordance (39/39 states, $r = +0.931, rho = +0.912$).
- *Melanoma, Pan-Cancer, HNSCC & PDAC Tier 1A Atlases*: `CELLxGENE_7b20c613` @gondal2025curated achieved $r = +0.962, rho = +0.940$ ($95.8%$ sign agreement, 46/48), `GSE120575` @sadefeldman2018defining achieved $r = +0.959, rho = +0.928$ ($84.2%$, 32/38), `GSE200996` @luoma2022molecular achieved $r = +0.963, rho = +0.933$ ($86.2%$, 25/29), and `GSE316195` @raufi2026singlenucleus achieved $r = +0.947, rho = +0.879$ ($94.4%$, 51/54).
- *Unified Multi-Cohort Tiers (1B, 2, and 3)*: `NSCLC-Unified` ($K = 105$) achieved $r = +0.969, rho = +0.929$ ($90.5%$ sign agreement, 95/105), `Melanoma-PanCancer-Unified` ($K = 86$) achieved $r = +0.958, rho = +0.948$ ($88.4%$, 76/86), `Unified-All9` ($K = 355$) achieved $r = +0.963, rho = +0.925$ ($85.9%$, 305/355), and the 42-state pan-cancer `Consensus-Meta42` reference achieved $r = +0.928$, Spearman $rho = +0.917$, and *$88.1%$ (37/42 states) directional sign concordance* ($p = 5 times 10^(-4)$).

