    *(a)* Two-objective Pareto landscape plotting cross-modality effect concordance (Pearson $r$ vs. single-cell `milopy` $overline("logFC")$) against multi-cohort predictive `ROC-AUC` across all 13 single-cell references (`#1`–`#13`, colored by Reference Tier 1A, 1B, 2, and 3 and sized by state count $K$), illustrating how `Consensus-Meta42` (`K = 42`) resolves the dimensionality–collinearity penalty of `Unified-All9` (`K = 355`).
    *(b)* Out-of-fold pan-cancer Random Forest Gini feature importance $I_k^("RF")$ regressed against univariate single-cell abundance magnitude $|overline("logFC")_k|$ across all 42 `Consensus-Meta42` states ($N = 1,015$). Six positive-residual outlier states—led by `#1` `M17` (`ISLR+COL5A2+ myCAF`, $I^("RF") = 0.0312$ despite $|overline("logFC")| = 0.45$), `M20` (`IL7R+CD40LG+ Trm`), `M04` (`GNLY+PRF1+ Eff. T`), `M29` (`JCHAIN+MZB1+ Plasma`), `M05` (`TRAF3+CD96+ Mem. T`), and `M30` (`MS4A1+CR2+ TLS B`)—exhibit disproportionate tree-split leverage indicative of non-linear conditional interactions.
  ]
) <fig-pareto-rf-outliers>

Crucially, regressing pan-cancer Random Forest Gini feature importance $I_k^("RF")$ against univariate single-cell effect magnitude $|overline("logFC")_k|$ across all 42 states (@fig-pareto-rf-outliers b) exposed a striking mechanistic anomaly: the single highest-importance feature in the entire 42-state Random Forest was *`M17: ISLR+COL5A2+ myCAF`* ($I_("M17")^("RF") = 0.0312$), despite `M17` exhibiting only a modest marginal single-cell shift ($overline("logFC") = -0.45$). Alongside `M17`, five additional states—`M20` (`IL7R+CD40LG+ Trm`), `M04` (`GNLY+PRF1+ Eff. T`), `M29` (`JCHAIN+MZB1+ Plasma`), `M05` (`TRAF3+CD96+ Mem. T`), and `M30` (`MS4A1+CR2+ TLS B`)—lay far above the linear main-effect trendline. Why do decision trees split heavily on `myCAF`, `TLS B`, `Plasma`, and `GNLY+ Eff. T` states beyond what their univariate main effects predict?

Evaluating trial-adjusted multiplicative logistic epistasis ($z_(i j)$) and Friedman–Popescu 2D Random Forest partial-dependence curvature ($H_(i j)$) across both the focused $8 times 8$ outlier/anchor submatrix (@fig-nonlinear-interactions-8) and the exhaustive $42 times 42$ (`1,764`-entry, $binom(42, 2) = 861$ unique-pair) pan-atlas ecosystem (@fig-nonlinear-interactions-all42) answered this question decisively, uncovering two opposing non-linear circuit motifs across human solid tumors:

