Stratifying all $N = 1,015$ pan-cancer clinical trial patients into $3 times 3$ conditional tertile regimes confirmed the clinical magnitude of this stromal gate at both focused (@fig-nonlinear-interactions-8 b) and pan-atlas (@fig-nonlinear-interactions-all42 c) scales:
- *Focused Stromal Exclusion Gate* (`M04 + M30 + M29` gated by `M17 myCAF + M32 M2-TAM`): When the myofibroblastic/M2-macrophage barrier lies in the lowest tertile (*Permissive Low-Stroma `T1`*), rising lymphoid-TLS infiltration drives objective RECIST response rates from $26.9%$ ($n = 145$) in `T1` to $32.5%$ ($n = 77$) in `T2` and *$61.5%$* ($n = 117$) in `T3` (conditional correlation $r = +0.286$). At *Moderate Stroma (`T2`)*, the effector slope flattens ($30.8% -> 32.3% -> 34.5%, r = +0.052$). At *High `myCAF/M2` Stroma (`T3`)*, clinical response is completely extinguished across all lymphoid infiltration tiers ($17.8% -> 24.8% -> 20.7%, r = +0.002$)—patients with abundant bulk lymphoid/TLS transcripts but high myofibroblastic stroma respond at less than one-third the rate ($20.7%$ vs. $61.5%$) of equally inflamed low-stroma tumors.
- *Pan-Atlas 42-State Gating* (26 $hat(beta)_("meta") > 0$ Responder States gated by 16 $hat(beta)_("meta") < 0$ Barrier States): Aggregating across the entire 42-state ecosystem (@fig-nonlinear-interactions-all42 c) reproduced the exact same conditional phase transition across $N = 1,015$ patients: objective response climbs from $26.9%$ ($n = 130$) to $31.2%$ ($n = 93$) to *$59.5%$* ($n = 116$, conditional $r = +0.283$) in *Permissive Low-NR TME (`T1`)*, attenuates to $22.9% -> 37.5% -> 38.9%$ ($r = +0.126$) in *Moderate NR TME (`T2`)*, and collapses to *$20.9% -> 24.8% -> 20.2%$* ($r = -0.078$) in *Excluded High-NR TME (`T3`)*. Together, these results explain both why `Consensus-Meta42` achieves superior discrimination and why non-linear Random Forests excel in zero-shot cross-trial `LOCO` transfer: predicting checkpoint efficacy requires jointly resolving pro-inflammatory `CXCL13+ Tex` / `TLS B` / `Plasma` / `M1-TAM` recruitment *and* the `myCAF` / `Mat. CAF` / `MDSC` stromal barrier that gates their functional access to tumor parenchyma.
